{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JAScipyY48C8kassemTuqX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/` holds per-utility implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles output formatting. `magefiles/` drives the build/generation pipeline (excluded from code generation).\n\n**Implementation state** (from source_code): All foundational packages exist (`pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`). Three utilities have complete implementations: `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, plus `cmd/version`. All code is present in the repo.\n\n**Current release**: Releases 00.0 through 01.2 are fully implemented (code exists for all use cases). **Release 01.3 (du)** is the earliest incomplete release — specs are complete but no source code exists. This is the next work item.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe only remaining work in the scoped releases [00.0, 01.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3] is **cmd/du** (rel01.3-uc001-du). All other use cases have source code. Per P2, implementation and tests must be split into separate tasks. With a 1-task limit, I propose the implementation task (canonical ordering: implementation before tests).\n\nDependencies: `pkg/sys` (Lstat with Blocks field) and `pkg/format` (HumanSize) already exist. No blocking dependencies.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/du: Implement core directory traversal and disk usage reporting (prd008-du R1, R2, R3, R5)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd008-du.yaml (PRD for du -- all requirements, flags, exit codes, edge cases; if path not found, locate the du PRD in docs/specs/product-requirements/)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.3-uc001-du.yaml (end-to-end execution path for du)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component pattern, pkg/sys/ for file metadata, pkg/format/ for size formatting)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference pattern for main/run structure, flag.NewFlagSet with ContinueOnError, error formatting to stderr, exit code handling)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference pattern for installSIGPIPEHandler using signal.Notify on syscall.SIGPIPE)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (Lstat function returning FileInfo with Blocks int64 field -- 512-byte units from st_blocks)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go (fillFromStat showing how Blocks is populated from syscall.Stat_t)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (HumanSize function with HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true} for -h flag output)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"du command: recursive directory traversal, block accumulation, size display flags (-h, -k, -b), aggregation flags (-s, -c, -a, -d), error handling, SIGPIPE handler\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement recursive directory traversal that walks each argument path depth-first using os.ReadDir + pkg/sys.Lstat, accumulates disk usage from the Blocks field (st_blocks in 512-byte units), and reports per-directory totals to stdout in the format '<size>\\\\t<path>\\\\n'. Default size unit is 1024-byte blocks (Blocks * 512 / 1024, rounded up with ceiling division). When no arguments are given, default to '.'. Use the same main()/run(args []string) int/os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:])) pattern as cmd/wc and cmd/cat. Each directory total includes its own allocation plus all descendants. Implements prd008-du R1.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement size display flags: -h (human-readable output via pkg/format.HumanSize with HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true}, converting from bytes = Blocks * 512), -k (1024-byte blocks -- this is the default), -b combined with --apparent-size (use apparent file size FileInfo.Size in bytes instead of disk allocation Blocks * 512). When -h is active, pass the byte value to HumanSize and print the result instead of a numeric block count. Implements prd008-du R2.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement aggregation and filtering flags: -s/--summarize (display only a total for each command-line argument, equivalent to -d 0), -c/--total (print a grand total line labeled 'total' after processing all arguments), -a/--all (write size counts for all files not just directories), -d/--max-depth=N (print the total for a directory only if it is N or fewer levels below the command-line argument; 0 means only the argument itself). Implements prd008-du R3.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement error handling and signal management: exit 0 when all arguments succeed, exit 1 if any error occurs (permission denied, nonexistent path, read failure). Print errors to stderr in the format 'du: <path>: <error>' using os.PathError unwrapping (same pattern as cmd/wc printFileError and cmd/cat printFileError). Continue processing remaining arguments and subdirectories after per-entry errors. Install SIGPIPE handler using signal.Notify on syscall.SIGPIPE that calls os.Exit(0) (same pattern as cmd/cat installSIGPIPEHandler). Implements prd008-du R5.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the run(args []string) int entry point pattern from cmd/wc and cmd/cat. Parse flags with flag.NewFlagSet('du', flag.ContinueOnError) with fs.SetOutput(os.Stderr).\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use manual recursion with os.ReadDir + pkg/sys.Lstat rather than filepath.WalkDir. This enables bottom-up size accumulation where each directory's total includes all descendants, matching GNU du's depth-first reporting order (children printed before parent).\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true}) for -h flag. Do not reimplement size formatting. Import pkg/sys for Lstat and pkg/format for HumanSize -- these are the only internal package dependencies.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Differential tests against GNU reference binary 'gdu' (Homebrew coreutils) will be implemented in a separate du_test.go task. This task produces only cmd/du/main.go. The reference binary name 'gdu' follows the g-prefix convention used by cmd/wc (gwc) and cmd/cat (gcat).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/du/main.go exists and compiles with 'go build ./cmd/du/' producing a working binary with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running the binary with no flags on a directory produces tab-separated 1024-byte block counts and paths on stdout, one line per directory, with children printed before parents (depth-first order).\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Flags -h, -k, -b, -s, -c, -a, and -d are all accepted by the flag parser and produce correctly formatted output: -h uses pkg/format.HumanSize, -s suppresses per-subdirectory output, -c appends a total line, -a includes files, -d limits output depth.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"The binary exits 0 on success and 1 on any error. Errors are written to stderr in 'du: <path>: <message>' format. Permission-denied on a subdirectory reports the error and continues traversal of remaining entries without halting.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":76518,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":76518},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"460d6e5b-80c0-41b8-8e05-e5ace93232f3","uuid":"99b012bd-8c8f-4680-bb40-ec751c7720ce"}
